<h2>Meal Preparation</h2>

<div class="meal-box">

<h3>Importance of Meal Preparation</h3>

<p>
Meal preparation is an important part of nutrition for people who go
to the gym because it helps them stay consistent with their diet and
fitness goals. Preparing meals in advance ensures that they eat the
right amount of protein, carbohydrates, and healthy fats needed to
support muscle growth, recovery, and energy.
</p>

<p>
Meal prep also helps people stay consistent with their nutrition plan.
Preparing meals ahead of time makes healthy food available and helps
control portion sizes.
</p>

<p>
Another benefit of meal preparation is that it saves time and money.
Cooking several meals at once reduces daily preparation time and can
be more affordable than buying restaurant or takeout meals.
</p>

</div>

<div class="meal-box">

<h3>Workout and Meal Preparation</h3>

<p>
Regular exercise is an essential part of a healthy lifestyle and works
hand in hand with proper meal preparation. A balanced exercise routine
should include strength training, cardiovascular activities,
flexibility exercises, and adequate rest.
</p>

<p>
Cardiovascular exercises such as brisk walking, jogging, running,
cycling, swimming, and jump rope improve heart and lung function.
Core exercises strengthen the abdominal and lower back muscles,
while flexibility exercises can improve range of motion.
</p>

</div>

